---
title: Core API
description: Framework-neutral exports for adapters, tooling, and low-level runtimes.
---

`spektral` and `/core` expose the same framework-neutral runtime surface.

| Export | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `defineMaterial`, `resolveMaterial` | Validate and resolve material declarations |
| `createCurrentWritable` | Subscribable value with synchronous `.current` access |
| `createFrameRegistry` | Task, stage, invalidation, and profiling engine |
| `createSpektralRuntimeLoop` | Renderer lifecycle and RAF orchestration |
| `loadTexturesFromUrls` | Framework-neutral URL texture loader |
| `toSpektralErrorReport` | Normalize unknown errors |
| `ShaderPass`, `BlitPass`, `CopyPass` | Post-scene render passes |
| `ComputePass`, `PingPongComputePass` | Pre-scene compute passes |
| `PingPongShaderPass` | Pre-scene fragment-feedback pass |

The entrypoint also exports the related public types: materials, resources, frame registry, runtime loop, errors, passes, render targets, color pipeline contracts, and the experimental render-graph snapshot schema. Graph exports include `SpektralGraph`, `RenderGraphSnapshot`, its node, resource, access, edge, and reason types, and `RENDER_GRAPH_SNAPSHOT_SCHEMA_VERSION`.

`SpektralGraph.getSnapshot()` is exposed by adapter contexts rather than as a standalone core
instance. The returned schema-version-1 snapshot is deeply frozen and cached until the plan
changes. Its node and resource IDs are opaque and stable only for one renderer lifetime.

Compute resource exports include `ComputeResourceMap`, every descriptor variant, texture view selection, current/initial versions, and typed external texture, view, buffer, and sampler references.

Use an adapter entrypoint when an application needs `FragCanvas` or hooks. Use core for custom adapters, headless validation, shader tooling, and direct runtime integration.
